{
  /* Typechecks the TypeScript under scripts/, which no project covered until
     2026-09-30 — see the `needsGemma` arity bug fixed alongside this, which
     survived for months because `tsc` never read the call site.

     A GLOB with one exclusion, deliberately not a list of trees: a new
     `scripts/foo/` is then covered the day it appears, rather than waiting for
     someone to remember this file exists. That is the same failure this project
     was added to stop.

     Options come from tsconfig.server.json via `extends` so they cannot drift.
     Three deliberate additions:

     - "strict": the server project does not set it. New coverage starts strict
       rather than being tightened later against a moving target, and it is what
       makes an implicitly-any callback parameter an error. Note the asymmetry:
       scripts/ imports broadly from src/server, so those files are strict-checked
       HERE while tsconfig.server.json still checks them without it. They are
       strict-clean today; the tidier end state is `strict` in the server project
       and none here.
     - "allowJs" with "checkJs" off, so `scripts/lib/natural-sort.mjs` infers
       instead of erroring TS7016. It is the one .mjs helper these trees import
       that has no .d.mts — 20 others under scripts/ do, and a declaration wins
       over the source where both exist.
     - excluding scripts/lib, whose 13 files are ALL *.test.ts and carry 62 errors
       between them. No non-test .ts lives there, so nothing is skipped by leaving
       it out: what these trees import from scripts/lib is .mjs. Those tests are
       covered by no project at all — tsconfig.test.json takes only test files
       under src plus scripts_tests — and want their own pass.

     Careful editing these comments: a glob containing a star-slash closes the
     block early, which is why the exclusion above is described in words. */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.server.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.scripts.tsbuildinfo",
    "strict": true,
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["scripts/lib/**"]
}
